  body: "# Reasonable work-seeking steps in the actual week\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    guidance assesses reasonable work-seeking steps in the week concerned and warns that the steps recorded
    in an agreement will not necessarily be those giving the best prospects in every week.\n\n## Scope
    and exceptions\n\nDMG 21571 preserves treated and joint-claim-exempt cases. The actual weekly circumstances,
    evidence and full labour-market provisions remain necessary. This is not a fixed checklist, an instruction
    to take an unsuitable job or a current UC/New Style JSA claimant commitment rule.\n\n## Inspected
    source passages\n\n- [DMG 21571, PDF page 156](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=156)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 21: Jobseeker’s Allowance Labour market questions, special conditions for JSA(Cont)
    and jobseeking periods.\n- [DMG 21572, PDF page 156](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=156)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 21: Jobseeker’s Allowance Labour market questions, special conditions for JSA(Cont)
    and jobseeking periods.\n- [DMG 21573, PDF page 156](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=156)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 21: Jobseeker’s Allowance Labour market questions, special conditions for JSA(Cont)
    and jobseeking periods.\n- [Inspected continuation, PDF page 158](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=158)
    — context for the selected paragraph.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch21`: PDF SHA-256 `d9fc5e120f85cb69386c9009d97ed2b33844523429224eded21be3c5003693e2`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `82d02218371af05595ac356e9c2f48f5434eb15adf97f0d0d057294c33b099c1`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-claimant-commitment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly compares agreed steps with what is reasonable in the actual
      week, so the agreement is relevant evidence rather than an automatic weekly pass or failure.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch21/0156
      quote: "21573 Details of what the claimant has agreed to do to satisfy the ASE test will be in the
        claimant's JSAg.\nBut claimants must in each week take the steps that give them their best chance
        of getting employment\nand this might not always be the same as the steps agreed in the JSAg."
      locator: DMG 21573
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-availability
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source allows treated actively-seeking and treated-availability findings to
      differ for a particular set of circumstances.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch21/0158
      quote: "21585 Claimants may be treated, for a particular set of circumstances, as\n\n\n1. ASE but
        not available for employment or\n\n\n2. available for employment but not ASE."
      locator: DMG 21585
